{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git status --short --branch && git log --oneline --decorate -12 && git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD && git diff --find-renames --check origin/main...HEAD && gh issue view 7 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --comments && gh pr view 12 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json number,title,state,baseRefName,headRefName,mergeable,reviewDecision,commits,files,body,comments'","aggregated_output":"author:\tmrkkucharski\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nFix cycle 1: no reviewer comment was left on the issue/PR to work from (checked issue comments, PR comments, and PR reviews — all empty), so I reviewed the implementation against the acceptance criteria myself.\n\nFound and fixed a real bug: `reascript/vgt_initialize.lua`'s `write_settings` unconditionally rewrote the sidecar as `schema_version: 1` on every apply/re-apply, silently deleting any `analysis` block `vgt analyze` had already written. Since the `.vgt` sidecar is meant to be the single shared contract between the ReaScript apply action and the Python analysis CLI, re-applying Phase 0 (e.g. to switch the reference track) was destroying analysis work already done — the reader/writer sides of the contract weren't actually symmetric.\n\nFix: the action now reads back any existing `analysis` object before overwriting the sidecar and round-trips it verbatim, only advancing `schema_version` to 2 once analysis exists (a fresh apply with no prior analysis still writes schema 1, so the existing Phase 0 live-verification procedure is unaffected). Verified the Lua brace-balancing extraction logic against nested-object JSON with a standalone interpreter, and confirmed the resulting output is valid JSON in both the with- and without-analysis cases.\n\nAll 13 existing tests still pass; this is a REAPER-only code path so it isn't covered by the Python test suite (same limitation as the rest of the Lua apply action).\n--\n{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"body\":\"Closes #7\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nSee issue #7 for details.\",\"comments\":[],\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-07-18T11:52:44Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"marekkucharski@mini.local\",\"id\":\"\",\"login\":\"\",\"name\":\"Marek Kucharski\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Sonnet 5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-07-18T11:52:44Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Adds `vgt analyze [project]`, which resolves the reference track's\\nsource-file path from the phase 0 sidecar/RPP and detects\\ntempo/key/sections/chords (stub detectors for now; real DSP/ML lands\\nin later sub-issues of #7).\\n\\nExtends the .vgt sidecar to schema_version 2 with an `analysis` block\\n(one cached entry per stage, plus provenance) while keeping all phase\\n0 fields intact and readable. Each stage entry caches on an\\ninput-hash + settings-hash pair, so re-running only recomputes stages\\nwhose audio or settings changed, and a `human_verified` flag lets a\\nmanual correction survive re-runs untouched.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat: add vgt analyze CLI stage and .vgt sidecar schema v2\",\"oid\":\"ccda5d5fa0c461544747d5dbb24d9882bd8ebfdc\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-07-18T11:53:03Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"marekkucharski@mini.local\",\"id\":\"\",\"login\":\"\",\"name\":\"Marek Kucharski\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Sonnet 5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-07-18T11:53:03Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs: document vgt analyze and the corrections mechanism\",\"oid\":\"434a9c964cca779427e8dd5d03ff3f4b78b5c7fd\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-07-18T11:58:41Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"marekkucharski@mini.local\",\"id\":\"\",\"login\":\"\",\"name\":\"Marek Kucharski\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Sonnet 5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-07-18T11:58:41Z\",\"messageBody\":\"The ReaScript apply action unconditionally rewrote the sidecar as\\nschema_version 1 on every run, silently deleting any `analysis` block\\n`vgt analyze` had already written. Since the sidecar is the single\\nshared contract between the DAW action and the Python CLI, re-applying\\nPhase 0 (e.g. to pick a different reference track) was destroying\\nanalysis work. The action now reads back and round-trips any existing\\n`analysis` object, only advancing schema_version to 2 once one exists.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix: preserve analysis block across Phase 0 re-apply\",\"oid\":\"3ec72dc64abf108adb9858942025397147abc5f0\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"additions\":15,\"deletions\":2,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"reascript/vgt_initialize.lua\",\"additions\":40,\"deletions\":3,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/__init__.py\",\"additions\":4,\"deletions\":2,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/analysis.py\",\"additions\":111,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/cli.py\",\"additions\":10,\"deletions\":2,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/project.py\",\"additions\":19,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/sidecar.py\",\"additions\":90,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"},{\"path\":\"tests/test_analysis.py\",\"additions\":133,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"}],\"headRefName\":\"issue-7-phase-1-analysis-foundation-vgt-sidecar\",\"mergeable\":\"UNKNOWN\",\"number\":12,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Phase 1: analysis foundation + .vgt sidecar schema v2\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
